<%# Wraps one configuration section's controls so they can be locked while SLA tracking is off for %>
<%# this project. LAYOUT partial — locals: project, locked. %>
<%# %>
<%# A <fieldset disabled> rather than a `disabled` attribute per input, for two reasons: it reaches %>
<%# every descendant control including the section's own Save button and any field added later %>
<%# without anyone remembering this rule, and — the part that actually matters — a control inside a %>
<%# disabled fieldset is NOT SUBMITTED, so a locked section cannot be posted even by hand. The %>
<%# server is still the authority (SlaPoliciesController re-checks on save); this is the UI half. %>
<%# %>
<%# Disabled, never hidden: the values have to stay readable while tracking is off, because seeing %>
<%# what a project WOULD measure is exactly how someone decides whether to turn tracking back on. %>
<%# %>
<%# The banner is rendered whether or not the section is locked (hidden when it isn't) so %>
<%# sla_policy_form.js can reveal it the moment the General switch is flipped, without having to %>
<%# build markup in JavaScript. %>
<%= render 'sla_policies/locked_notice', project: project, locked: locked %>
<fieldset class="sla-lock-fieldset" data-sla-lock <%= 'disabled' if locked %>>
  <%= yield %>
</fieldset>
